Let me analyze this problem:

1. Find the maximum possible bitwise OR of any subset of `nums`. Since all nums[i] >= 1, the maximum OR is achieved by OR-ing all elements together.
2. Count the number of non-empty subsets whose OR equals this maximum.

Constraints: n <= 16, so we can enumerate all 2^16 = 65536 subsets, or use DFS/backtracking.

Approach 1: Brute force over all subsets using bitmask enumeration.
- Compute maxOr = OR of all elements.
- For each mask from 1 to 2^n - 1, compute OR of elements in the mask, count if equals maxOr.

That's 65536 * 16 operations = ~1M, fine.

Approach 2: DFS with (index, currentOr) and count when index == n. Or better, count during recursion: if currentOr == maxOr at any point... Actually simpler: DFS(i, or) — when i == n, check or == maxOr.

Approach 3: DP over OR values: dp[or] = number of subsets achieving that OR. Iterate through nums, new_dp[x | num] += dp[x], plus dp[x] stays (not including num). Start with dp[0] = 1. Answer is dp[maxOr]. Since maxOr <= 2^17 or so (nums[i] <= 10^5 < 2^17 = 131072), the OR of all is < 2^17. So dp array of size 131072 works. Actually 10^5 < 131072 = 2^17. So max OR < 2^17.

Let me write the simple bitmask enumeration:

```java
class Solution {
    public int countMaxOrSubsets(int[] nums) {
        int maxOr = 0;
        for (int x : nums) maxOr |= x;
        int n = nums.length;
        int count = 0;
        for (int mask = 1; mask < (1 << n); mask++) {
            int or = 0;
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                if ((mask & (1 << i)) != 0) or |= nums[i];
            }
            if (or == maxOr) count++;
        }
        return count;
    }
}
```

This is O(2^n * n) = 65536 * 16 ≈ 1M operations, well within limits.

Alternatively, a slightly faster DFS approach:

```java
class Solution {
    private int maxOr = 0;
    private int count = 0;
    private int[] nums;

    public int countMaxOrSubsets(int[] nums) {
        this.nums = nums;
        for (int x : nums) maxOr |= x;
        dfs(0, 0);
        return count;
    }

    private void dfs(int i, int or) {
        if (i == nums.length) {
            if (or == maxOr) count++;
            return;
        }
        dfs(i + 1, or | nums[i]);
        dfs(i + 1, or);
    }
}
```

