Let me analyze this problem:

1. We have m students and m mentors (m ≤ 8)
2. Each student must be paired with exactly one mentor (perfect matching)
3. We want to maximize the sum of compatibility scores

Since m ≤ 8, we can use bitmask DP or brute force over permutations (8! = 40320 permutations, each with up to 8 students × 8 questions = manageable).

Approach 1: Bitmask DP
- Precompute score[i][j] = compatibility between student i and mentor j
- dp[mask] = maximum score sum when mentors in mask are assigned to the first popcount(mask) students
