```java
class Solution {
    public int maxCompatibilitySum(int[][] students, int[][] mentors) {
        int m = students.length;
        int n = students[0].length;

        // Precompute compatibility scores
        int[][] score = new int[m][m];
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
                int s = 0;
                for (int k = 0; k < n; k++) {
                    if (students[i][k] == mentors[j][k]) s++;
                }
                score[i][j] = s;
            }
        }

        // Bitmask DP: dp[mask] = max score when mentors in mask assigned to first popcount(mask) students
        int size = 1 << m;
        int[] dp = new int[size];
        for (int mask = 0; mask < size; mask++) {
            int i = Integer.bitCount(mask); // next student to assign
            if (i >= m) continue;
            for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
                if ((mask & (1 << j)) == 0) {
                    int newMask = mask | (1 << j);
                    dp[newMask] = Math.max(dp[newMask], dp[mask] + score[i][j]);
                }
            }
        }

        return dp[size - 1];
    }
}
```

This is O(2^m * m) for the DP plus O(m^2 * n) for precomputing scores. With m = 8, that's 256 * 8 = 2048 DP operations. Very fast.

