- Values go up to 10⁵, so squares/products go up to 10¹⁰ → must use `long`.
- Efficient counting: build a frequency map of the pair-array `b`. For each `x`, for each distinct value `v` in `b`, if `x² % v == 0`, let `w = x² / v`. If `w == v`, add `C(count[v], 2)`; if `w > v` (to count each pair once), add `count[v] * count[w]` when `w` exists in the map.

