Looking at this problem:

- **Key insight**: We need to check if any *suffix* of the stream matches a word. If we build a trie of the **reversed** words, then checking suffixes becomes: walk the trie starting from the most recently added character backwards.
- **Bounded buffer**: Since no word exceeds `maxLen` characters, we only need to keep the last `maxLen` characters of the stream. Each query walks at most `maxLen` (≤ 200) trie nodes, so with ≤ 4·10⁴ queries this is very fast.

**Approach**:
1. Constructor: insert each word *reversed* into a trie, marking end-of-word nodes; track the maximum word length.
2. `query(letter)`: append the letter to a buffer (trimming it to at most `maxLen` chars), then traverse the trie from the last character backwards. If we hit a null child, no suffix matches — return false. If we reach a node marked as a word end, some suffix matches — return true.

Verification with Example 1 (`words = ["cd","f","kl"]`, reversed trie branches: `d→c`, `f`, `l→k`): after queries `a,b,c,d` the buffer is `"cd"`; walking `d` then `c` finds the word end → true. Query `f` matches single-char word → true. Query `l` with buffer `"kl"` walks `l` then `k` → true. All outputs match.

```java
class StreamChecker {

    private static class Node {
        Node[] children = new Node[26];
        boolean isWord;
    }

    private final Node root = new Node();
    private final StringBuilder stream = new StringBuilder();
    private int maxLen = 0;

    public StreamChecker(String[] words) {
        for (String w : words) {
            if (w.length() > maxLen) {
                maxLen = w.length();
            }
            Node cur = root;
            for (int i = w.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
                int c = w.charAt(i) - 'a';
                if (cur.children[c] == null) {
                    cur.children[c] = new Node();
                }
                cur = cur.children[c];
            }
            cur.isWord = true;
        }
    }

    public boolean query(char letter) {
        stream.append(letter);
        if (stream.length() > maxLen) {
            stream.deleteCharAt(0);
        }
        Node cur = root;
        for (int i = stream.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            cur = cur.children[stream.charAt(i) - 'a'];
            if (cur == null) {
                return false;
            }
            if (cur.isWord) {
                return true;
            }
        }
        return false;
    }
}

/**
 * Your StreamChecker object will be instantiated and called as such:
 * StreamChecker obj = new StreamChecker(words);
 * boolean param_1 = obj.query(letter);
 */
